00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.500
The Boy — He has seen the sun
rise for the last time in Great
Bend — before taking the long,
long journey.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:19.250
"Mother, Mildred has promised to
come to the city and marry me —
just as soon as I've made good."

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.250
"Oh Harold, it would just
break my heart if you failed —"

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.000
"— I know I'll get nothing
but good news from you."

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:42.250
After a few months — "Limpy
Bill," The Boy's pal — one
pocketbook between them —
usually empty —

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:10.750
"What good is a lavalier without
a chain — she can't sew it on."

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:19.750
"I know it, Bill. I'll get the
chain, all right, the very first
money I can scrape up."

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.750
"Oh, pal — she's just got to
believe that I'm successful —
until I am."

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.750
"If we'd had more records I
could 'a' got the chain, too."

00:07:52.500 --> 00:08:00.000
The Boy was always early — he
couldn't have cared more for his
job if it had been a position —

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:13.000
"Keep on bein' earlier every
mornin', son, an' you'll be
President — or a night
watchman."

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:07.250
The longest year The Boy ever
spent — in thirty minutes.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:40.000
"Hey, you! It's all your fault.
If you don't get me back in ten
minutes I'll lose my job."

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.000
"I dunno, my watch has stopped."

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.750
"Stop the car at the
next corner, please."

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:27.250
"You'll be lucky if you
don't get fired for this!"

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:03.750
Mr. Stubbs — Head Floorwalker.
Muscle-bound — from patting
himself on the back —

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:08.250
Saturday brings two great events
— a half holiday, and the pay
envelope.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:22.250
"I think I like the first
pattern you showed me best."

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.000
"No — no — just a
sample, please."

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:42.000
"If it ain't Jim Taylor of Great
Bend! You old rascal! How you
have got on in the world —"

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:24.250
"Bill, you'd be surprised at the
pull I've got with the cops. I
can do anything — and get away
with it."

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:40.500
"I'll prove it to you. I'll
kneel down behind, and you shove
him over backwards. Then watch
me square it."

00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:33.750
"YOU'LL DO TIME FOR THIS! THE
FIRST TIME I LAY EYES ON YOU
AGAIN, I'LL PINCH YOU!"

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:11.000
"Shucks, you ain't seen nothin'
— I could climb one sixteen
stories high — blindfolded."

00:26:10.250 --> 00:26:13.750
Direct from "Tiffany's"
— via Silverstein & Son.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:37.750
"Don't you think it's dangerous
for a young man to be alone in
the city, with so much money?"

00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:46.500
"If I were you, I wouldn't
wait. I'd go to him right away."

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:52.000
"I'll do it. I'll surprise him."

00:26:56.750 --> 00:26:59.250
Mother instinct was right.
The Boy is in great danger.

00:28:01.500 --> 00:28:03.750
"— 8-9-10-OUT!"

00:28:22.250 --> 00:28:24.500
"Is this a yard and a half?"

00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:05.750
"Who dropped that
FIFTY DOLLAR BILL?"

00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:54.750
"Go and adjust your apparel,
young man. I shall report you to
the General Manager."

00:30:06.500 --> 00:30:10.250
"Very well, Mr. Stubbs. I'll
send for the young man."

00:30:55.250 --> 00:31:00.750
The most wonderful city The Girl
has ever seen — except Great
Bend.

00:31:08.250 --> 00:31:11.500
"Wrap this, please. The
lady is in a hurry!"

00:31:40.750 --> 00:31:46.000
"We're so proud of you, Harold,
and your w-o-n-d-e-r-f-u-l
position."

00:32:49.750 --> 00:32:56.000
"Must I personally supervise
every sale that is made in this
department?"

00:33:51.250 --> 00:33:57.250
"Now observe me closely. I will
illustrate the correct form of
salesmanship."

00:34:24.500 --> 00:34:29.750
"Oh yes. Our European buyer
wants my advice. This is most
important."

00:35:20.750 --> 00:35:31.000
"The idea of working in your
shirt sleeves! Think of the
shock to your customers — women
of culture and refinement."

00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:43.250
"Another complaint of this
nature, and we will have to get
along without your services.
That will be all."

00:36:18.250 --> 00:36:23.000
"I'm just dying to see your
office — please let me look."

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:58.500
"But Harold, I DID want
to see your office."

00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:13.750
"Well then — just a peek. But
you must promise not to stay."

00:38:11.500 --> 00:38:17.000
"BOY! Empty this basket — don't
let me have to remind you
again."

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.750
"Oh Harold, let me ring one.
And see who it will bring in."

00:39:11.250 --> 00:39:12.750
"STUBBS —"

00:39:16.750 --> 00:39:25.500
— I don't wish to be annoyed by
any more of your petty
complaints about personal
appearance —

00:39:28.500 --> 00:39:32.500
"— You know, you're no
collar ad yourself."

00:39:35.250 --> 00:39:37.750
"That will be all."

00:40:20.750 --> 00:40:23.750
"Fire drill. I try
them out every day."

00:40:30.750 --> 00:40:33.750
"Open your mouth and
shut your eyes —"

00:40:48.250 --> 00:40:51.250
"She's fainted! Get
some water, quick!"

00:41:48.250 --> 00:41:54.500
"And just think — you've made
money enough already for our
little home."

00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:11.750
"I must have left my purse in
your office. Won't you please
get it for me."

00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:14.750
"I'd give a thousand dollars —
to anyone — for a new idea — one
that would attract an enormous
crowd to our store."

00:43:50.500 --> 00:44:00.000
"Will you give me a thousand
dollars, sir — if — if — I can
draw hundreds of people to our
store?"

00:44:11.750 --> 00:44:21.979
"Let's give the boy a chance.
Think of the publicity in the
newspapers. The De Vore
Department Store will be all

00:44:21.989 --> 00:44:24.000
over the front pages."

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:05.000
"Will you climb the Bolton
Building — twelve floors — for
five hundred dollars?"

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:15.750
"Say, for five hundred dollars
I'd climb to Heaven, an' hang by
my heels from the pearly gates."

00:45:29.250 --> 00:45:39.250
"Mrs. Van Buren, have this young
man send your car home. I'll be
so glad to have you ride over to
the club with me."

00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:49.250
"Darling, dreams do come true.
We'll be married tomorrow."

00:45:51.750 --> 00:45:57.500
"I'll send you to the hotel in
the car. Meet me here tomorrow
at 3."

00:46:04.750 --> 00:46:12.750
"Take this young lady to her
hotel — and Mrs. Van Buren says
you're through for the day."

00:46:15.250 --> 00:46:19.000
"Good-bye, darling. Tomorrow
will be our lucky day."

00:47:22.750 --> 00:47:29.000
"Look! Thish guy ain't got any
face. They mustta run outta
ink."

00:48:20.500 --> 00:48:23.750
"Where does this
bird start from?"

00:48:52.500 --> 00:48:55.750
"You lay low. Maybe
I can ditch him."

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:50.250
"Meet my lady frien'
— from the Follies."

00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:44.000
"Go on, you can do
it. Only o-n-e floor."

00:53:02.250 --> 00:53:06.250
"I'M the Mystery Man. I
wanted to surprise you."

00:55:39.750 --> 00:55:44.000
"You'll have to go one more
floor — till I ditch the cop."

00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:30.250
"Why dontcha take that net
off? It's in your way."

01:00:17.000 --> 01:00:21.000
"You've gotta keep on goin'
— till I ditch the cop."

01:01:24.750 --> 01:01:29.250
"Young man, don't you know
you might fall and get hurt?"

01:02:32.750 --> 01:02:37.000
"Come on. Just this one
floor, an' you'll be through."

01:02:39.250 --> 01:02:42.000
"You BE THERE, or
I will be THROUGH."

01:05:30.250 --> 01:05:36.000
"Great! You got the right idea,
kid. That's the best one you've
pulled yet."

01:06:56.500 --> 01:07:03.500
"Make this next floor faster.
I'm having a little difficulty
in ditching the cop."

01:07:19.750 --> 01:07:24.000
"Get out of here! Don't you
know the dog might fall?"

01:12:28.750 --> 01:12:32.250
"I'll be right back —
soon as I ditch the cop."

01:13:09.250 --> 01:13:11.750
